# Testing

Primary suite lives in `app/test_features.py` (feature groups) plus `app/tests.py` and `app/test_production_config.py`.

## Patterns to follow

- Reuse `FeatureDataMixin` and `make_user(..., role=User.Role.*)` with password `Pass1234!` for consistency.
- Use `reverse()` for URL names; API tests use `APIClient` + JWT via `RefreshToken.for_user(user)`.
- Time-sensitive appointment tests: use `timezone.now()` and helpers like `window()` — do not hard-code wall-clock dates.
- Mock external services (`patch` on `app.services` Drive/n8n helpers) instead of calling real webhooks in tests.

## Adding coverage

- Name test classes by feature area (`*Tests`) and one behavior per test method.
- For production settings behavior, prefer `SimpleTestCase` + `override_settings` as in `test_production_config.py`.
- After changes, run: `python manage.py test app --verbosity 2`

## CI expectations

- Tests run with PostgreSQL (`DATABASE_URL` in workflow), `DEBUG=False`, and secure cookies disabled for the test client (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`).
